---
import BlockLayout from '../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import library from '../data/object-library.json';
import '../styles/object-library.css';
const jsonLd = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'CreativeWork', name: library.name, url: library.canonical, description: library.disclosure, dateCreated: library.date, genre: 'Concept catalog and lending demo', isAccessibleForFree: true };
---
<BlockLayout title="El Segundo Object Library · Borrow an idea" description={library.description} image="/images/object-library/social.png" themeColor="#f5f1e8" immersive isolated showNetworkStrip={false} jsonLd={jsonLd} alternates={[{type:'application/json',href:'/object-library.json',title:'Object Library — concept catalog and product brief'}]}>
  <div class="ol" data-object-library>
    <a class="ol-skip" href="#catalog">Skip to the objects</a>
    <header class="ol-header">
      <a class="ol-wordmark" href="/">POINTCAST <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="ol-brand" href="#top"><span class="ol-mini-glasses" aria-hidden="true">⌐◨-◨</span> OBJECT LIBRARY</a>
      <nav aria-label="Object Library"><a href="#catalog">The objects</a><a href="#demo">Try the demo</a><a href="/weather-atlas/">Weather atlas ↗</a></nav>
    </header>
    <div>
      <section class="ol-hero" id="top" aria-labelledby="ol-title">
        <div class="ol-hero-copy"><p class="ol-kicker">EL SEGUNDO / SIX SMALL POSSIBILITIES</p><h1 id="ol-title">Good things.<br/>Less owning.<br/><span>More trying.</span></h1><p class="ol-dek">An object library for the way we live.<br/>Borrow an idea. Try a ritual. Make it better.</p><div class="ol-actions"><a href="#catalog" class="ol-button ol-blue">Meet the objects <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="ol-text-link" href="#demo">Rehearse a loan ↗</a></div><p class="ol-small ol-hero-boundary"><span class="ol-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> CONCEPT CATALOG + BROWSER DEMO<br/>No physical inventory or borrowing service.</p></div>
        <figure class="ol-hero-art"><img src="/images/object-library/family.svg" alt="Six original object characters with square glasses: a coral focus dial, yellow lamp, blue pocket companion, green shade clip, mint window signal and pink rain sleeve" width="1200" height="1000" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption><span>THE EVERYDAY SIX</span><span>ORIGINAL CONCEPT ILLUSTRATIONS / 01</span></figcaption></figure>
      </section>
      <aside class="ol-status" aria-label="Prototype status"><strong>AN IDEA YOU CAN TRY.</strong><p>These objects are proposed designs. The demo creates a card on this device; it does not reserve, submit, charge, arrange pickup or promise a working product.</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></aside>
      <section class="ol-section ol-intro" aria-labelledby="ol-intro-title"><div><p class="ol-kicker">01 / UTILITY, BEFORE MORE STUFF</p><h2 id="ol-intro-title">Start with a need.<br/><span>End with a better idea.</span></h2></div><div><p class="ol-lead">The best object might be the one you only need sometimes. Or the one you can improve before anyone makes a hundred of them.</p><p>This El Segundo concept connects a shared object shelf to a proposed Local Object Factory. A useful local loop: name a small problem, try a modest answer, record what happened and repair or rethink it.</p><a class="ol-text-link" href="#factory">Follow the local loop ↗</a></div></section>
      <section class="ol-section ol-catalog" id="catalog" aria-labelledby="ol-catalog-title">
        <div class="ol-section-head"><div><p class="ol-kicker">02 / THE CONCEPT CATALOG</p><h2 id="ol-catalog-title">Six objects.<br/><span>A hundred little uses.</span></h2></div><p>Each character has one clear job and one question. Try the suggested ritual with something you already have before imagining a new device.</p></div>
        <div class="ol-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter by everyday use"><button type="button" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All six <span>06</span></button>{library.uses.map(use=><button type="button" data-filter={use.id} aria-pressed="false">{use.name}</button>)}</div>
        <p class="ol-sr" role="status" data-filter-status>Showing all six concept objects.</p>
        <div class="ol-object-grid">{library.objects.map(object=><article class:list={['ol-object', `ol-${object.color}`]} id={object.id} data-object={object.id} data-utility={object.utility}><div class="ol-specimen"><span>OL / {object.number}</span><span>CONCEPT</span></div><div class="ol-object-picture"><img src={`/images/object-library/${object.image}`} alt={`${object.name}, an original ${object.type.toLowerCase()} character concept with square glasses`} width="600" height="540" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="ol-object-copy"><p class="ol-kicker">{object.type}</p><h3>{object.name}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></h3><p class="ol-object-tagline">{object.tagline}</p><p>{object.description}</p><details><summary>Use / experiment / limits <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><dl><dt>Try the ritual</dt><dd>{object.ritual}</dd><dt>First experiment</dt><dd>{object.experiment}</dd><dt>Proposed construction</dt><dd>{object.materials}</dd><dt>Know the boundary</dt><dd>{object.boundary}</dd></dl></details><div class="ol-weather-link"><span aria-hidden="true">☀</span><p>{object.weather}<a href={`/weather-atlas/?season=${object.season}#living`}>Explore the weather atlas ↗</a></p></div><button type="button" class="ol-pick" data-pick={object.id} aria-pressed="false">Try {object.name} in the demo <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></button></div></article>)}</div>
        <noscript><p class="ol-noscript">All six concepts, their uses and the notebook below work without JavaScript. The local demo and filters need JavaScript.</p></noscript>
      </section>
      <section class="ol-atlas-callout" aria-labelledby="ol-atlas-title"><div class="ol-atlas-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="ol-sun">☀</span><span class="ol-coast-line"></span><span class="ol-map-dot">25<br/><small>MILES</small></span><span class="ol-cloud">≈</span></div><div><p class="ol-kicker">ONE PLACE. MANY WAYS TO LIVE.</p><h2 id="ol-atlas-title">Let the season<br/><span>shape the ritual.</span></h2><p>A coastal walk, a warm inland afternoon, an evening at home: the same object can have a different use. The Weather &amp; Living Atlas brings historical context, seasonal patterns and practical choices into the picture.</p><a href="/weather-atlas/" class="ol-button ol-cream">Open the 25-mile atlas <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="ol-small">Historical patterns support planning. Check current weather, heat, air quality and route advisories before acting.</p></div></section>
      <section class="ol-section ol-demo" id="demo" aria-labelledby="ol-demo-title">
        <div class="ol-section-head"><div><p class="ol-kicker">03 / A LENDING REHEARSAL</p><h2 id="ol-demo-title" tabindex="-1">Try the loop.<br/><span>Keep the learning.</span></h2></div><p>Choose an object, describe a use, create a demo card and return with one observation. Everything stays in this browser. No real loan or submission is created.</p></div>
        <ol class="ol-steps" aria-label="Demo lending steps"><li data-step="choose" aria-current="step"><b>01</b><span>Choose an idea</span></li><li data-step="plan"><b>02</b><span>Plan a use</span></li><li data-step="card"><b>03</b><span>Rehearse a loan</span></li><li data-step="reflection"><b>04</b><span>Return a learning</span></li></ol>
        <noscript><p class="ol-noscript">The lending rehearsal is disabled without JavaScript so no form can submit your notes. Read the object rituals above to explore the idea.</p></noscript>
        <div class="ol-demo-grid">
          <form class="ol-plan" data-plan-form>
            <label for="ol-choice">Your concept object</label><select id="ol-choice" disabled name="objectId"><option value="">Choose one of the six</option>{library.objects.map(object=><option value={object.id}>{object.name} / {object.type}</option>)}</select>
            <label for="ol-use">What would you try?</label><select id="ol-use" disabled name="useId">{library.uses.map(use=><option value={use.id}>{use.name}</option>)}</select>
            <div class="ol-form-pair"><div><label for="ol-duration">A small trial</label><select id="ol-duration" disabled name="duration"><option value="twenty-minutes">Twenty minutes</option><option value="one-walk">One walk</option><option value="one-evening">One evening</option><option value="one-day">One day</option></select></div><div><label for="ol-season">Season in your plan</label><select id="ol-season" disabled name="season"><option value="winter">Winter</option><option value="spring">Spring</option><option value="summer">Summer</option><option value="fall">Fall</option></select></div></div>
            <label for="ol-intention">One thing you want to learn <span>(optional)</span></label><textarea id="ol-intention" disabled name="intention" rows="3" maxlength="400" placeholder="Would a physical start ritual make my first task easier?"></textarea>
            <button class="ol-button ol-blue" type="submit" disabled data-make-card>Create my demo borrow card <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><p class="ol-small">Use an existing object or a paper sketch. No hardware, inventory or pickup is supplied.</p>
          </form>
          <div class="ol-demo-card" data-demo-card>
            <div class="ol-card-empty" data-card-empty><span class="ol-empty-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌐◨-◨</span><p class="ol-kicker">YOUR CARD GOES HERE</p><h3>A little experiment.<br/>A useful answer.</h3><p>Pick an object to begin. This is a rehearsal of how a future library might work.</p></div>
            <div data-card-content hidden><div class="ol-card-top"><span>OBJECT LIBRARY / DEMO ONLY</span><span data-card-status>REHEARSED</span></div><img data-card-image src="/images/object-library/turn.svg" alt="" width="600" height="540"/><div class="ol-card-body"><p class="ol-kicker" data-card-type></p><h3 data-card-name></h3><dl><dt>Your use</dt><dd data-card-use></dd><dt>Trial / season</dt><dd data-card-trial></dd><dt>What to learn</dt><dd data-card-intention></dd></dl><p class="ol-card-boundary">DEMO ONLY · No reservation, due date, pickup, charge or submission.</p></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <form class="ol-reflection" data-reflection-form hidden><div><p class="ol-kicker">THE RETURN / KEEP ONE OBSERVATION</p><h3>What would you<br/><span>change next time?</span></h3><p>After a paper rehearsal or a real-life ritual with your own belongings, note what helped and what did not. These notes are yours; no maker receives them.</p></div><div><label for="ol-outcome">Did the ritual help?</label><select id="ol-outcome" disabled name="outcome"><option value="not-tried">Not tried yet / just rehearsing</option><option value="helped">Helped with this use</option><option value="mixed">Some parts helped</option><option value="not-helpful">Did not help this time</option></select><label for="ol-observation">One observation <span>(optional)</span></label><textarea id="ol-observation" disabled name="observation" rows="3" maxlength="400" placeholder="The dial needs a clearer off state. The paper version was enough…"></textarea><button type="submit" disabled class="ol-button ol-green">Complete the demo return <span aria-hidden="true">↺</span></button></div></form>
        <div class="ol-demo-tools"><p class="ol-storage" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" data-demo-status>Demo notes save only in this browser when storage is available.</p><div><button type="button" data-export-demo disabled>Download my demo notes ↓</button><button type="button" data-clear-demo>Clear this browser’s demo</button></div></div>
      </section>
      <section class="ol-section ol-factory" id="factory" aria-labelledby="ol-factory-title"><div><p class="ol-kicker">04 / CONNECTED TO LOCAL OBJECT FACTORY</p><h2 id="ol-factory-title">From shelf<br/>to bench.<br/><span>And back again.</span></h2><p>{library.factory.premise}</p><p class="ol-small">{library.factory.status}. The workshop connection is a proposed workflow. Demo notes are not sent to a factory.</p></div><ol class="ol-loop">{library.factory.loop.map((step,i)=><li><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h3>{step}</h3><b aria-hidden="true">{i===5?'↺':'↘'}</b></li>)}</ol></section>
      <section class="ol-section ol-notebook" id="product-notebook" aria-labelledby="ol-notebook-title"><div><p class="ol-kicker">05 / THE OPEN PRODUCT NOTEBOOK</p><h2 id="ol-notebook-title">A proposal.<br/><span>With the work<br/>still visible.</span></h2><p>A product brief and business-case outline for the next decision. Research is proposed, not completed; no invented demand or operating economics.</p><a href="/object-library.json" class="ol-text-link">Read the full machine edition ↗</a></div><div class="ol-notebook-content"><details open><summary>Product brief <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><dl><dt>Problem / audience</dt><dd>{library.productBrief.problem} {library.productBrief.audience}</dd><dt>This release</dt><dd>{library.productBrief.mvp}</dd><dt>Before a physical pilot</dt><dd>{library.productBrief.futureGate}</dd><dt>What to measure</dt><dd>{library.productBrief.success}</dd><dt>Out of scope</dt><dd>{library.productBrief.nonGoals}</dd></dl></details><details><summary>Business-case outline <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><dl><dt>Hypothesis</dt><dd>{library.businessCase.hypothesis}</dd><dt>Costs to model</dt><dd>{library.businessCase.costs}</dd><dt>Possible operating models</dt><dd>{library.businessCase.model}</dd><dt>Decision rule</dt><dd>{library.businessCase.decision}</dd><dt>Evidence needed</dt><dd>{library.businessCase.evidence}</dd></dl></details><details><summary>Research method / artwork provenance <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Object utility is a design hypothesis, developed from everyday use cases. No interviews, product trials, measured performance or demand study have been completed. Weather context comes from the linked atlas’s source and method appendix. The next research step would compare paper rituals with existing belongings, using consenting adults and explicit observations.</p><p>{library.provenance.creator}. {library.provenance.reference} {library.provenance.affiliation}</p><p>These original character SVGs are dedicated to <a href={library.provenance.cc0}>CC0 1.0 ↗</a>. <a href={library.provenance.nouns}>Nouns cultural reference ↗</a>. No token, wallet or ownership claim is involved.</p><a href="/images/object-library/provenance.json">Read illustration provenance ↗</a></details></div></section>
    </div>
    <footer class="ol-footer"><div><span class="ol-mini-glasses" aria-hidden="true">⌐◨-◨</span><p>Borrow an idea.<br/>Return a better one.</p></div><p>EL SEGUNDO / CONCEPT 01<br/>INDEPENDENT POINTCAST DESIGN</p><nav aria-label="More PointCast"><a href="/weather-atlas/">Weather &amp; Living Atlas ↗</a><a href="/object-library.json">Machine edition ↗</a><a href="/">Back to PointCast ↗</a><a href="#top">Back to top ↑</a></nav></footer>
  </div>
  <script>
    import library from '../data/object-library.json';
    import { initObjectLibrary } from '../scripts/object-library.mjs';
    const setup = () => initObjectLibrary(document.querySelector('[data-object-library]'), library);
    setup();
    document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', setup);
  </script>
</BlockLayout>
